{"id":"62ab684fdaba39000b6a2a08","slug":"francis-picabia-moret-sur-long-en-hiver-1","title":"Moret-sur-Long, en hiver","artists":["Francis Picabia"],"date":"ca. 1907","medium":"Oil on canvas","dimensions":"21 1/2 × 25 5/8 in","image":"kApBHIDY85hKQavAwhptVg","c":["#433f36","#95886f","#b5b393"],"said":[{"k":"writer","q":"The world of art is a richer, more complicated, more unpredictable place because of him.","by":"Ann Umland","via":"M.S. Rau, on Artsy"},{"k":"note","q":"Painted circa 1907, the work, entitled Moret-sur-Long, en hiver, represents a period of early exploration for the artist. Having met the two sons of the legendary Impressionist Camille Pissarro in 1902, Picabia eagerly took up his brush to paint his own landscape scenes executed en plein air.","by":"M.S. Rau, on Artsy"}],"events":[{"k":"made","y":"1907","c":1,"q":"ca. 1907","o":1,"s":[0]},{"k":"made","y":"1907","c":1,"q":"Painted circa 1907","o":1,"s":[1]},{"k":"listed","y":"2022-06-16","who":"M.S. Rau","n":"listed by the gallery","ll":[29.9576,-90.0649],"w":"New Orleans, US","p":"new-orleans-us","pr":"office","o":3,"s":[0]},{"k":"exhibited","y":"2022-10-22","e":"2023-01-07","t":"Revolutionaries: The Impressionists and Post-Impressionists","v":"M.S. Rau","ll":[29.9576,-90.0649],"w":"New Orleans, US","p":"new-orleans-us","pr":"venue","o":2,"s":[0]}],"sources":[{"name":"Artsy","url":"https://www.artsy.net/artwork/francis-picabia-moret-sur-long-en-hiver-1"},{"name":"M.S. Rau, on Artsy","url":"https://www.artsy.net/artwork/francis-picabia-moret-sur-long-en-hiver-1"}],"threads":[],"asof":"2026-10-01"}